---
layout: base.njk
title: "Potential DPRK Profiles"
description: "LinkedIn profiles matching heuristic signals associated with DPRK IT-worker persona accounts, held under human review before any connection to these operations is stated."
permalink: "/remote-workers/candidates/"
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
extra_head: '<script src="/assets/js/table-filter.js" defer></script>'
---
{#
  src/remote-workers/candidates/index.njk — the public face of the
  candidate-generation workflow in scripts/scan-candidates.js and
  src/_data/iocs/candidates.json.

  THIS PAGE DOES NOT NAME A LEAD. It renders only candidates whose `status` is
  "under-review": a human opened the profile under an authenticated session
  and judged it worth continued attention. Entries at "lead" (heuristic match
  only, not yet opened) and "false-positive" (checked and cleared) are read
  from the same file for the summary counts below but never rendered: a lead
  is a real person's name attached to nothing but a title and a URL pattern,
  and publishing that list would be exactly the weak-heuristic accusation this
  workflow exists to prevent. A "confirmed" row is no longer a potential
  profile and is not listed here either; its indicators stay in the Remote
  Workers search (scripts/lib/candidates.js).

  The rows come from the candidatePages global, already in the page's default
  order: highest confidence first, then by name. Each row's name opens its own
  page (candidate-page.njk), which carries the review note and sources the
  table has no room for.
#}
{% set active_tab = "candidates" %}
{% set queue = iocs["candidates"] %}
{% set published_candidates = candidatePages %}
{% set lead_count = 0 %}
{% set fp_count = 0 %}
{% for candidate in queue.candidates %}
  {% if candidate.status == "lead" %}
    {% set lead_count = lead_count + 1 %}
  {% elif candidate.status == "false-positive" %}
    {% set fp_count = fp_count + 1 %}
  {% endif %}
{% endfor %}

<section>
  <h1>Potential DPRK Profiles</h1>
  {% include "partials/profiles-tab-bar.njk" %}
  <p>
    Profiles that match the screening signals of DPRK IT-worker personas and
    have been opened by a reviewer. None is presented as a confirmed operator;
    see the note below the table.
  </p>
  <p class="form-hint">
    {{ published_candidates | length }} published{% if lead_count %}, {{ lead_count }} awaiting review{% endif %}{% if fp_count %}, {{ fp_count }} cleared{% endif %}.
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  {% if published_candidates.length %}
  {% set tableFilter = { target: "#candidates-table", noun: "profiles", page: limits.list, id: "candidate-search-input", label: "Search profiles", placeholder: "Name, account, indicator or signal" } %}
  {% include "partials/table-filter.njk" %}
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table class="results-table" id="candidates-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Persona name</th>
          <th scope="col">Profile</th>
          <th scope="col">Indicators</th>
          <th scope="col">Confidence</th>
          <th scope="col">Account created</th>
          <th scope="col">Network</th>
          <th scope="col">Claims</th>
          <th scope="col">Line type</th>
          <th scope="col">Photograph</th>
          <th scope="col">Signals</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {% for candidate in published_candidates %}
        {% set facts = candidate.facts | default({}, true) %}
        <tr id="candidate-{{ candidate.slug }}">
          <td><a href="{{ candidate.path }}">{{ candidate.display_name }}</a></td>
          <td class="candidate-links">{% set candidateFact = "profile" %}{% include "partials/candidate-fact.njk" %}</td>
          <td>{% set candidateFact = "indicators" %}{% include "partials/candidate-fact.njk" %}</td>
          <td>{% set candidateFact = "confidence" %}{% include "partials/candidate-fact.njk" %}</td>
          <td class="cell-date">{% if facts.account_created %}{{ facts.account_created }}{% else %}&mdash;{% endif %}</td>
          <td>{% set candidateFact = "network" %}{% include "partials/candidate-fact.njk" %}</td>
          <td>{% set candidateFact = "claims" %}{% include "partials/candidate-fact.njk" %}</td>
          <td>{% set candidateFact = "line" %}{% include "partials/candidate-fact.njk" %}</td>
          <td>{% set candidateFact = "photo" %}{% include "partials/candidate-fact.njk" %}</td>
          <td>{% set candidateFact = "signals" %}{% include "partials/candidate-fact.njk" %}</td>
        </tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  {% include "partials/table-filter-more.njk" %}
  {% else %}
  <p><em>No candidate has cleared authenticated review yet.</em></p>
  {% endif %}
</section>

<section>
  <h2>How a profile ends up here</h2>
  <p>
    Candidates are surfaced by search queries and marketplace scans, recorded
    as unconfirmed leads, and published here only after a reviewer opens the
    profile in a signed-in session and reads the details that distinguish a thin
    persona from a real applicant. A profile that is confirmed leaves this list;
    its indicators stay in the <a href="/remote-workers/">Remote Workers</a>
    search.
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  {% set disclaimer = {
    title: "Unconfirmed leads under review",
    preset: "not-proof",
    body: 'Each row was read by a reviewer, and its confidence is this site&rsquo;s own screening score, not a source&rsquo;s. If an entry concerns you, see <a href="/guidance/#listed">the guidance for listed people</a>.'
  } %}{% include "partials/disclaimer.njk" %}
</section>
